# Sol plan -> Terra build -> Sol review
For every non-trivial coding task:
1. Invoke sol-planner once before editing.
2. Verify the returned plan against repository evidence.
3. Implement with the Terra parent.
4. Run relevant tests, linting, type checks, and builds.
5. Inspect the final diff.
6. Invoke sol-reviewer once and fix blocking findings.

The parent model is GPT-5.6 Terra with ordinary medium/default reasoning; the
CLI may control exact effort, so do not claim it was hard-pinned.
